The code statements that lead to the bug are:
timer_delete(&priv->command_timer);
timer_delete(&priv->tx_lockup_timer);
Reason:
These non-synchronous timer deletions allow timer callbacks (lbs_cmd_timeout_handler, lbs_tx_lockup_handler) to execute after lbs_free_adapter returns, accessing freed memory because the containing structure is freed immediately after by lbs_cfg_free().

The code statements that fix the bug are:
timer_delete_sync(&priv->command_timer);
timer_delete_sync(&priv->tx_lockup_timer);
Reason:
Using timer_delete_sync ensures any running timer callback completes before the timer is deleted, preventing use-after-free when the structure is subsequently freed.

